WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.635
15 million web

00:00:01.447 --> 00:00:02.531
servers on one

00:00:02.343 --> 00:00:03.486
VM with smoltcp

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:04.571
DPDK

00:00:05.094 --> 00:00:06.438
A tongue-in-cheek but

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.358
technical walkthrough

00:00:07.169 --> 00:00:08.065
of running over

00:00:07.877 --> 00:00:09.256
15 million tiny

00:00:09.068 --> 00:00:10.141
web servers on

00:00:09.953 --> 00:00:10.895
one 1-core

00:00:11.422 --> 00:00:12.330
Starting from a

00:00:12.141 --> 00:00:13.473
10-line C server

00:00:13.545 --> 00:00:14.452
the author hits

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:15.172
limits one by

00:00:14.983 --> 00:00:15.502
one

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:17.023
ephemeral port ranges

00:00:17.165 --> 00:00:18.497
kernel socket memory

00:00:18.332 --> 00:00:19.252
and the cost

00:00:19.064 --> 00:00:20.089
of syscalls

00:00:20.606 --> 00:00:21.631
The kernel stack

00:00:21.443 --> 00:00:21.985
ran out of

00:00:21.797 --> 00:00:22.740
RAM at about

00:00:22.552 --> 00:00:24.414
2.5 million servers

00:00:24.521 --> 00:00:25.641
with smoltcp an

00:00:25.465 --> 00:00:26.702
idle server costs

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:29.084
about 620 bytes and the run

00:00:28.908 --> 00:00:30.417
reached 16 million

00:00:30.942 --> 00:00:31.956
Full story on

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:32.663
the dashboard
